  "result": "I'd put it in a neutral shared location (e.g. `shared/formatCurrency.js` or `common/utils/`) that neither team owns, so both `reports/` and `billing/` import from it without creating a dependency on each other's folder \u2014 that's the standard way to avoid the cross-module coupling you're worried about without duplicating logic. The main tradeoff with copying instead is drift: a rounding/locale bug fixed in one copy silently stays broken in the other, and you now have two things to keep in sync forever. Copy-paste only makes sense if you actually expect the formatting rules to diverge between reports and billing \u2014 if it's truly the same logic, a shared home is worth the minor governance overhead of picking who maintains it.",
